     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi all,<br>\r\n<br>\r\nI am running open occ models like the following:  (fm30&lt;- colext(~1, ~1, ~scale(warea), ~1, occ.umf))  <br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Notice I am scaling\r\nthe continuous covariate(warea) within the formula.  I saw in Richard&#39;s\r\nreply to a previous thread <span> </span>(<span>Model predictions when scaling covariates</span> , from\r\nMarch 2011)  that when you use &quot;predict&quot; after a model such as\r\nthis, the backtransformation/rescaling is already performed.  I want the backtransformed/original scale values for the extinction intercept and beta(warea)-- and don&#39;t know how to get those using predict?  I was using something like this (beta(warea) code only for brevity)  and receiving output that appeared to be backtransformed and unscaled:</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\n </p><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\"> </span><span style=\"color:blue\">warea.ext&lt;-backTransform(linearComb(fm30,type=&quot;ext&quot;,coefficients=c(0,1)))\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">warea.ext\r\n</span>Backtransformed linear combination(s) of Extinction estimate(s)\r\n\r\n Estimate     SE LinComb (Intercept) scale(warea)\r\n   0.0039 0.0134   -5.54           0            1\r\n</pre></span><br><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"64\"><colgroup><col style=\"width:48pt\" width=\"64\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.0pt;width:48pt\" height=\"20\" width=\"64\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"></span></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\"><br></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt;text-align:left\" height=\"20\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"></span><br></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\"><br></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">However, when compared to output from the model summary I noticed that while the parameter estimates are the same, the standard error estimates here do NOT correspond with the  backtransformed estimates I get from that output (see below).  The SEs are very different-- which method is correct (if either??).  <br><br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">Extinction (logit-scale):\r\n             Estimate   SE     z P(&gt;|z|)\r\n(Intercept)     -4.32 2.33 -1.85  0.0639\r\nscale(warea)    -5.54 3.46 -1.60  0.1092<br><br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">plogis(-5.54)\r\n</span>[1] 0.00391117    #same parameter estimate as above\r\n<span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">plogis(3.46)\r\n</span>[1] 0.969528       #DIFFERENT SE estimate from above<br></pre></span></pre></span><br></pre></span><br><br>Thanks for any help with this!<br>Tamara Pandolfo<br><br><br><br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><br><br><br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><br><br><br><br><br></pre></span><br></pre></span><br></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\"><br></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n</div>"
