   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:Verdana;color:#000000;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div>hi Tamara,<br>\r\n<br>\r\nthis may not be very helpful, but: you can&#39;t directly compare the SE. In particular, you can&#39;t do plogis(SE_hat) ! I assume that one is on the logit scale and the other on the probabilty scale, but I never understood how one can get a &quot;non-asymmetric&quot; SE on\r\n the latter. After all, the SE is symmetric on the link scale of the analysis, which is the logit here, so how can one get a single SE for a backtransformed estimate ? That has always puzzled me in MARK also.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nRegards  --  Marc<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div><font face=\"Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;font-size:16px\">\r\n<hr>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Tahoma\" size=\"2\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a> [<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a>] on behalf of Tamara Pandolfo [<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tjpa...@ncsu.edu</a>]<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 10 September 2013 21:26<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [unmarked] Re: Backtransformation of scaled covariate --different standard errors?<br>\r\n</font><br>\