   "subject": "Re: [unmarked] Backtransformation of scaled covariate --different standard errors?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>hi Tamara,</div><div> The reason for this is because the variance of a function of a parameter is not simply the function of the variance UNLESS the function is linear.  In the present case, the function is the inverse-logit function and unmarked uses a delta approximation to compute the variance.</div>\r\n<div> if x is your random variable with var(x)  and your transformation is:</div><div> </div><div> y = exp(x)/(1+exp(x))</div><div> </div><div> then the delta approximation yields:</div><div> </div><div> var(y) = (exp(x)/[  (1+exp(x) )^2 ])^2   * var(x)</div>\r\n<div> </div><div> so, in the example you provided, the SE is the square-root of the expression above:</div><div><br>&gt; exp(-5.54)/((1+exp(-5.54))^2) * 3.46<br>[1] 0.01347972<br>&gt; </div><div> </div><div>regards</div><div>\r\nandy</div><div><br> </div><div> </div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Sep 10, 2013 at 3:17 PM, Tamara Pandolfo <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tjpa...@ncsu.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi all,<br>\r\n<br>\r\nI am running open occ models like the following:  (fm30&lt;- colext(~1, ~1, ~scale(warea), ~1, occ.umf))  <br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Notice I am scaling\r\nthe continuous covariate(warea) within the formula.  I saw in Richard&#39;s\r\nreply to a previous thread <span> </span>(<span>Model predictions when scaling covariates</span> , from\r\nMarch 2011)  that when you use &quot;predict&quot; after a model such as\r\nthis, the backtransformation/rescaling is already performed.  I want the backtransformed/original scale values for the extinction intercept and beta(warea)-- and don&#39;t know how to get those using predict?  I was using something like this (beta(warea) code only for brevity)  and receiving output that appeared to be backtransformed and unscaled:</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\n </p><span style=\"font:13px/15px &quot;Lucida Console&quot;;text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;border-collapse:separate;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"margin:0px;line-height:1.2;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;outline-style:none\">\r\n<span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\"> </span><span style=\"color:blue\">warea.ext&lt;-backTransform(linearComb(fm30,type=&quot;ext&quot;,coefficients=c(0,1)))\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">warea.ext\r\n</span>Backtransformed linear combination(s) of Extinction estimate(s)\r\n\r\n Estimate     SE LinComb (Intercept) scale(warea)\r\n   0.0039 0.0134   -5.54           0            1\r\n</pre></span><br><table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"64\"><colgroup><col style=\"width:48pt\" width=\"64\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"width:48pt;min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\" width=\"64\"><span style=\"font:13px/15px &quot;Lucida Console&quot;;text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;border-collapse:separate;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"></span></td>\r\n\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\"><br></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:left;min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\"><span style=\"font:13px/15px &quot;Lucida Console&quot;;text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;border-collapse:separate;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"></span><br>\r\n</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\"><br></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">However, when compared to output from the model summary I noticed that while the parameter estimates are the same, the standard error estimates here do NOT correspond with the  backtransformed estimates I get from that output (see below).  The SEs are very different-- which method is correct (if either??).  <br>\r\n<br><span style=\"font:13px/15px &quot;Lucida Console&quot;;text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;border-collapse:separate;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"margin:0px;line-height:1.2;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;outline-style:none\">\r\nExtinction (logit-scale):\r\n             Estimate   SE     z P(&gt;|z|)\r\n(Intercept)     -4.32 2.33 -1.85  0.0639\r\nscale(warea)    -5.54 3.46 -1.60  0.1092<br><br><span style=\"font:13px/15px &quot;Lucida Console&quot;;text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;border-collapse:separate;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"margin:0px;line-height:1.2;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;outline-style:none\">\r\n<span style=\"font:13px/15px &quot;Lucida Console&quot;;text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;border-collapse:separate;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"margin:0px;line-height:1.2;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;outline-style:none\">\r\n<span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">plogis(-5.54)\r\n</span>[1] 0.00391117    #same parameter estimate as above\r\n<span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">plogis(3.46)\r\n</span>[1] 0.969528       #DIFFERENT SE estimate from above<br></pre></span></pre></span><br></pre></span><br><br>Thanks for any help with this!<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br>Tamara Pandolfo<br><br><br><br>\r\n<span style=\"font:13px/15px &quot;Lucida Console&quot;;text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;border-collapse:separate;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"margin:0px;line-height:1.2;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;outline-style:none\">\r\n<br><br><br><span style=\"font:13px/15px &quot;Lucida Console&quot;;text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;border-collapse:separate;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"margin:0px;line-height:1.2;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;outline-style:none\">\r\n<br><br><br><br><br></pre></span><br></pre></span><br></font></span></td><td><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n </font></span></td></tr><tr><td><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n </font></span><font color=\"#888888\"><tr style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\"><br></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</font></td></tr></tbody></table><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n</font></span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
