   "subject": "Re: [unmarked] Re: Backtransformation of scaled covariate --different standard errors?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>in response to Marc&#39;s email:  Marc suggests that computing a confidence interval for the back-transformed parameter (i.e., on the probabiliy scale) based on the approximate standard error would be unappealing because it would be symmetric.  An alternative approach is to compute the confidence interval on the linear scale and then back-transform the endpoints. </div>\r\n<div> </div><div> </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Sep 10, 2013 at 3:26 PM, Kery Marc <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">marc...@vogelwarte.ch</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Verdana;font-size:13px;direction:ltr\">\r\n<div>hi Tamara,<br>\r\n<br>\r\nthis may not be very helpful, but: you can&#39;t directly compare the SE. In particular, you can&#39;t do plogis(SE_hat) ! I assume that one is on the logit scale and the other on the probabilty scale, but I never understood how one can get a &quot;non-asymmetric&quot; SE on\r\n the latter. After all, the SE is symmetric on the link scale of the analysis, which is the logit here, so how can one get a single SE for a backtransformed estimate ? That has always puzzled me in MARK also.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nRegards  --  Marc<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div><font face=\"Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:16px\">\r\n<hr>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Tahoma\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a> [<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a>] on behalf of Tamara Pandolfo [<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tjpa...@ncsu.edu</a>]<br>\r\n\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 10 September 2013 21:26<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [unmarked] Re: Backtransformation of scaled covariate --different standard errors?<br>\r\n</font><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Sorry for the mess above, the second output was:<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br></div><div>\r\nThe problem being while parameter estimates are the same, the SEs are different.  Which method is correct?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nThanks!<br>\r\n<br>\r\nTamara\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid\" class=\"gmail_quote\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"64\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n<td style=\"width:48pt;min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\" width=\"64\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n<td style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n<td style=\"text-align:left;min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n<td style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n<td style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n<td style=\"min-height:15pt\" height=\"20\"><br>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div></div><div>\r\n<p></p>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;unmarked&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unmarked+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://group